Package: supermox-android
Architecture: all
Depends: supermox-ve,
         waydroid (>= 1.6.3),
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: squashfs-tools
Description: SuperMox Android layer (Waydroid container + Lawnchair)
 Runs a full Android system in a Waydroid LXC container on a SuperMox
 node, so the phone's own kernel and network stack stay in charge and
 Android is the userspace on top. Upstream waydroid only knows how to
 start through an init system SuperMox does not use, and the unit file
 it ships is dropped at install time; this package supplies the sysvinit
 service script for the container, the kernel module configuration for
 the binder mounts Android needs, and supermox-android-setup, which
 fetches the image, installs the pinned Lawnchair launcher (verified
 by sha256) and makes it the Android home app.
